/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it mostly works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_98727.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18011357/test_pr_98727.zip)\r\n\r\nI noticed some issues:\r\n\r\n- You can freely place your cursor around before writing in, which means you can accidentally start writing after the first character (e.g. with the mask `>AAAAA-AAAAA-AAAAA-AAAAA`):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3c16c3f-ed86-4db6-b1f3-ca256d7fdac8)\r\n\r\nThis may be convenient in certain cases, but it's also prone to misinputs, so I'd suggest not allowing placing the cursor within whitespace.\r\n\r\n- With the input mask `+99 99 99 99 99 99`, I can't enter the last character:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d3b3b013-520e-4a98-9759-293e539514ee)\r\n\r\nThis also occurs with the `>AAAAA-AAAAA-AAAAA-AAAAA` input mask, where the last section is limited to 4 characters instead of 5.\r\n\r\nIt works with the mask `+99 99 99 99 99 99;_` (or even `+99 99 99 99 99 99; ` with a trailing space), as setting a custom blank character fixes the issue (`+99 99 99 99 99 99;` doesn't work either). I can now enter the final digit:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fadc30da-f2a1-4e71-bfff-4c593abd6092)\r\n\r\n\r\n","